  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Chen Cheng tells Wooden Statue Lord Wu Guang that his master is heading to Crescent Moon Mound to challenge Yin Wu Que, and that Wu Guang has a close relationship with him and can lead the way. Wu Guang calls him Brother Yin and hesitates because Yin Wu Que is his good friend.",
      "chapters": [
        2167
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chen_cheng",
        "char_wu_guang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a thin body. After Hei Lou Lan’s punches he is covered in dust, one eye socket cracked and swollen purple with blurred vision.",
      "chapters": [
        2169
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hei Lou Lan challenges him in an intense fight. He uses Crescent Moon Thrust, Moon Rise, and moonblade killer moves, raising a waxing crescent moon that amplifies his moon path methods. He inherited the inheritance of an Olden Antiquity moon path Gu Immortal great expert and has a complete, stable combat system: destroyed or countered moon path moves feed dao marks into the crescent so it can grow toward a full moon and peak amplification. He judges he is not her match yet and tries to delay while retreating.",
      "chapters": [
        2169
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "moon-path-duel",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_crescent_moon_thrust",
        "move_moon_rise",
        "evt_era_olden",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A barrage of punches and kicks breaks his defense. He admits defeat in panic, and she stops when Wu Guang urges her to spare him. Lying on the ground under Wu Guang’s treatment, he tells Liu Chang and Liu Luo that Fairy Black Moon came to challenge him and he is not her match. He refuses Liu tribe’s repeated offer to become an external supreme elder, saying he is used to being alone. After she thrashes the Liu siblings, he joins her entourage so Liu tribe will not come for him and so he need not join a Huang Jin tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        2170
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-entourage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_liu_chang",
        "char_liu_luo",
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration notes that she defeated Chen Cheng and Yin Wu Que while challenging experts, that Liu Chang and Liu Luo failed to recruit him, and that he and other lone and demonic experts follow her on their own initiative under forceful Huang Jin recruitment pressure.",
      "chapters": [
        2188
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-moon-challenges",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
